  "assembly_notes": "The mechanism family owns its topology and matched compensation hardware. Every base provides one vertical swivel axis; every mechanism consumes it and provides one terminal pitch axis; every terminal consumes that pitch axis. Fork width, hub depth, cheek spacing, pivot-pin length and wrist clearance are derived before geometry emission. All 90 structural combinations are legal and require no compatibility gate. Segment-count records describe alternate joint graphs, not homogeneous N repetition.",
